  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes with 5 of 5 tests.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. Now a job's slot is freed whether it succeeds or fails, and the queue moves on to the next job. A job that throws synchronously, or returns a plain value instead of a promise, is also handled. Before, either one crashed the queue.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits until nothing is running.\n- **One job at a time after `resume()`:** `resume()` started a single job. It now starts jobs until every free slot is filled, and the same loop is used whenever a job finishes.\n\nI added three regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`, one per problem:\n- The queue keeps going after a rejected job and after a synchronous throw.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs, and resolves straight away when the queue is already idle.\n- With concurrency 4, `resume()` immediately runs 4 jobs, and no more than 4 run at once.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't seen them fail there. I haven't committed anything.",
